Digital Unix 4.0 have useradd and dxaccounts commands. The problem
with them is that if domainname is set, they assume that NIS is in
use, and they print error messages. If domainname is blank strig, they
assume that NIS is not in use, and they work correctly. I have
domainname set, but I don't use NIS. Since lot of applications expects
that hostname is just hostname whithout the name of domain, and that
domainname *is* set to the name of domain, I susspect that lot of
people out there have this problem (if they for this or that reason
need to use useradd instead of adduser command).

This behavior of useradd and dxaccount commands is certanly not
correct. The simple workaround would be to set domainname to blank
string before using useradd, and then recreating it after useradd has
done it's job, but this is realy a bad solution to the problem. Is
there any other workaround and/or patch for this?

